WEBVTT

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:22.122
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.626
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.697
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.301
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:43.343
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:54.117
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.558
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.996
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:07.067
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:14.735
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:43.770
Looks like that woman assigned us a crack pilot.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.001
STW-9000 has engaged the enemy units.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.776
Let's just hope that wolf keeps his sheepskin on.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.945
Bogie, start up the PSP.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:52.809
What are you planning?

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.849
He can't hold them off all on his own.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:59.580
I won't say I can take on half,
but I'll draw some of them off.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.821
Juliet, how far are we from our destination?

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.522
Who?

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.046
Pilot, that's you.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.993
You had J-something written
on your fuselage, right?

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.052
So starting today, you're Juliet. Respond.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.999
In direct distance, we are
approximately 1.5 kilometers away.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.568
However, we are currently engaging
in evasive maneuvers,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.433
so it is possible for that distance to grow.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:21.274
It's a bit too far to muscle our way in.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:21.933
Let's get off here.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:37.712
Here we go!

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:42.726
Breaking Through Enemy Lines

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:47.131
Juliet, lower your altitude as far as you can!

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.533
Once I'm out, make a crash
landing and offload the tank.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:56.266
Then you withdraw from
here at full power. Got it?

00:02:56.442 --> 00:03:00.970
I have been ordered to provide you
with support as much as possible.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.183
Deserting the frontline in
this situation would be...

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.276
You've still got a job to do, remember?

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.315
Job to do?

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:10.852
Yup. You better come back for us.
We've got roundtrip tickets here.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.521
Roger.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.261
Bogie, take care of everyone for me.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.663
Don't do anything reckless.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:17.561
I know.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.166
Okay, you two, see you down there.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.098
Yes.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.671
Say, we're thinking the same thing, aren't we?

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:25.194
Hmm?

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.173
She's at her cutest when she's acting reckless.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.909
Okay, guess I'll head out.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.682
Good. Follow me!

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.297
Do you suppose so?

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:56.833
The enemy's here.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.171
The enemy?

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.468
Is it The Third?

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.797
I don't know.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.035
Don't you sense them?

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:06.537
I'm sorry. I was too
engrossed in our conversation.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:08.537
I see.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.453
Is the enemy...

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.545
...just the one plane?

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.348
Yes.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.422
I see no escort force.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.425
I will be on the lookout outside.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.957
Would that be all right?

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.286
Please do that.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.432
They are not The Third?

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.250
Bogie, I've landed successfully!

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.184
Signal jamming, huh?

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.107
Please brace for impact.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.571
We will be crash landing in 60 seconds.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.914
Isn't your ground speed too fast, Juliet?

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.849
This is a normal combat approach.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.117
So she says.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.778
Are you addressing me?

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.847
You're the one being tossed out there.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:25.454
Calling anything "normal combat"
is mistaken to begin with.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.857
Combat isn't normal, it's abnormal.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.271
You okay?

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:42.500
Yes. But this is a first for me.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.513
The right engines?

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.381
It is only Engine 1. It will not affect our landing.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:52.508
Continuing the approach.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:56.322
If the worst should happen,
we'll make an emergency exit and land.

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.256
I don't really care.
I wish we could just hurry up with this.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.989
It's not in me to just sit still and take hits.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:02.980
Bogie?!

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.646
Blue Breaker...

00:07:31.184 --> 00:07:32.446
They are fine.

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:36.619
The transport plane dropped the tank,
then crash landed.

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.290
Currently, the tank is...

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:54.002
Signal flare confirmed.
Approximately 5 kilometers ahead.

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:56.405
It seems they are fine as well.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:59.042
Hurry. We've gotten pretty separated.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.054
Do we wait to meet up?

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.487
No, let's go.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.887
We've gotten this far.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:18.797
I'd hate to give our opponents time
to regroup while we poke along.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.130
There are too few of them.

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:27.607
Could they not be The Third, after all?

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:31.236
Their purpose may not be a military
operation, but to negotiate.

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:33.877
In that case, the issue of their numbers...

00:08:35.615 --> 00:08:37.640
That will not be allowed, Joganki.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:41.820
Because the negotiator is already here.

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.323
You. And only you.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:49.095
I've issued no other demands.

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.497
With regards to negotiations, that's true,

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:54.166
but what about everything else?

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.224
Everything else?

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:59.171
The temporary shutdown of the
Central Integrated Government...

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.240
...and the transfer of all authority.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.832
What happened to those demands?

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.410
Those were...

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.279
Since I came here,

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:09.282
you have not said anything to the
Central Integrated Government.

00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:10.214
Am I wrong?

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.575
I showed them I could use the wormhole driver!

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:16.122
You issued your demands to the
Central Integrated Government.

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:19.759
And demands always come with deadlines.

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:20.453
But you...

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.896
As long as the wormhole driver is in my control,

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:26.262
no one can touch me! Isn't that right?!

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:33.264
I still have my doubts.

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:34.771
About what?

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.369
Whether you will use that trump card...

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:43.872
Whether you have the will to use the
wormhole driver once again, Rona.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.927
There is a deadline.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:57.922
There is one.

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:18.247
Quiet, isn't it?

00:10:18.684 --> 00:10:20.242
There's no challenge in this.

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:23.389
Conventionally speaking, they should've
moved some of their forces...

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:25.914
...to where they expected us to land.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:28.921
It's the enemy you've been waiting for.

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.028
Where to?

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.732
I'm going to cut down their numbers.

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:36.131
Bogie, you keep your eyes out front.

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:38.097
I'll take care of the rear.

00:10:38.437 --> 00:10:39.802
You stay here.

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:41.638
Since you're a damn amateur.

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:46.809
Iks, I'm going to switch to combat deployment.

00:10:47.213 --> 00:10:48.646
Brace for impact.

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:50.783
To let her go without any objection,

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:52.978
it seems you must have faith in her as well.

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:57.986
To my knowledge, in situations like
this, she's a most reliable person.

00:11:21.414 --> 00:11:24.406
They're not taking us seriously if
they're not using their stealth coats.

00:11:25.051 --> 00:11:27.918
Or could our opponent be an amateur?

00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:51.976
They're a stone's throw away from us now.

00:11:52.645 --> 00:11:54.943
But they don't seem to be the Inspection Force.

00:11:55.414 --> 00:11:59.077
If you don't mind, please describe it
so I can understand the situation.

00:11:59.185 --> 00:12:00.482
All right.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.022
The enemy has one autonomous soldier...

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:04.887
...with a configuration that
differs from the military.

00:12:05.591 --> 00:12:07.684
My voice doesn't seem to reach it.

00:12:08.427 --> 00:12:10.793
It's a very pretty blue color.

00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:13.487
Blue Breaker...

00:12:14.767 --> 00:12:18.760
And one humanoid machine
that I've never seen before.

00:12:19.138 --> 00:12:21.402
This one's a manned weapon.

00:12:21.507 --> 00:12:22.974
It doesn't have an artificial brain.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.477
A PSP?

00:12:25.945 --> 00:12:28.880
I see, so that thing's called a PSP.

00:12:29.515 --> 00:12:33.975
Also, it's still a little ways away,
but there's a tank.

00:12:35.187 --> 00:12:38.315
If they're not the Inspection Force,
could they be mercenaries?

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:43.858
But would the Central Integrated
Government ever hire mercenaries?

00:12:43.929 --> 00:12:45.396
What do you think, Joganki?

00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:48.534
Joganki?

00:12:48.534 --> 00:12:50.024
Y-Yes?

00:12:50.169 --> 00:12:50.999
Is something the matter?

00:12:52.104 --> 00:12:52.900
No.

00:12:53.672 --> 00:12:56.470
A tank... and a PSP...

00:12:56.542 --> 00:12:57.668
It couldn't be...

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:06.783
I wonder if those autonomous
soldiers were the last of them.

00:13:06.852 --> 00:13:08.843
My motion sensors aren't picking up anything.

00:13:09.655 --> 00:13:11.054
Guess we'll give it a go, then.

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.459
Follow me. We're gonna
charge in there in one shot!

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:14.016
Wait.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:15.484
Something's coming.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.562
Holy! What kind of armor does that thing have?!

00:13:27.373 --> 00:13:28.067
Say...

00:13:28.874 --> 00:13:31.138
What's a multiped tank like?

00:13:32.044 --> 00:13:36.071
There was one among the
detachment I brought with me.

00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:38.984
They were primarily designed
to mop-up mobile weapons...

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:41.578
...like the autonomous soldiers.

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:45.590
Then this is as far as those two will get.

00:14:05.544 --> 00:14:07.012
What the heck is that guy?

00:14:07.012 --> 00:14:09.606
Land sweeper multiped tank.

00:14:10.015 --> 00:14:11.817
What a tongue-twister.

00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:12.875
So what're its weaknesses?

00:14:13.052 --> 00:14:14.280
None worth mentioning.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.884
It would be a different story if
we had an anti-tank chopper.

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:19.114
There's no point in wishing for
something we don't have.

00:14:19.592 --> 00:14:22.117
If anything, it's weak against
attacks from above or below.

00:14:22.294 --> 00:14:24.524
Its armor is thinnest in those areas.

00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:26.627
Standard anti-tank combat theory.

00:14:27.132 --> 00:14:28.656
Above and below, huh?

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:31.631
You take above. I'll attack it from below.

00:14:32.171 --> 00:14:33.305
What do you plan to do?

00:14:33.305 --> 00:14:34.431
Watch for my timing.

00:14:34.607 --> 00:14:36.632
You should probably be able to manage it.

00:15:44.176 --> 00:15:47.009
Awesome! That was perfect timing!

00:15:47.579 --> 00:15:49.479
How are you capable of doing such things?

00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:49.979
Huh?

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:53.743
I have been at the receiving
end of that sword once.

00:15:54.253 --> 00:15:55.982
Is it made of some special material?

00:15:56.355 --> 00:15:57.151
No...

00:15:57.656 --> 00:15:58.748
Then, how?

00:15:59.058 --> 00:16:01.327
Three meals a day and plenty of sleep.

00:16:01.327 --> 00:16:03.488
Plus daily training, I guess?

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.094
I see.

00:16:07.733 --> 00:16:09.496
I guess that was satisfactory.

00:16:33.158 --> 00:16:34.523
Rona Fauna.

00:16:38.063 --> 00:16:39.587
I never would have thought it.

00:16:39.898 --> 00:16:42.765
I guess tank armor can be cut through easily...

00:16:44.336 --> 00:16:46.566
By a little girl's sword like that.

00:16:46.939 --> 00:16:50.306
Why did you involve Honoka
in this, Fila Marique?!

00:16:53.779 --> 00:16:54.711
What's the matter?

00:16:55.247 --> 00:16:56.976
Why are you so agitated?

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.150
When you were so calm until just now...

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:04.019
Reading another's mind is not a
particularly commendable hobby.

00:17:04.556 --> 00:17:05.991
Though,

00:17:05.991 --> 00:17:11.663
if this massive system is ultimately
only useful to such an extent,

00:17:11.663 --> 00:17:13.028
that's rather sad.

00:17:13.499 --> 00:17:15.865
I see. You're right.

00:17:16.668 --> 00:17:18.795
It may be exactly as you say.

00:17:19.505 --> 00:17:23.942
Maybe in the end, it all exists only for you.

00:17:25.144 --> 00:17:27.813
I'd like it if you would tell me soon.

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:30.247
What is your true objective?

00:17:30.416 --> 00:17:33.819
Even combining your special
abilities with this system,

00:17:33.819 --> 00:17:35.921
the Central Integrated Government
is too much for you to tackle.

00:17:35.921 --> 00:17:38.651
Even you should be aware of that.

00:17:41.527 --> 00:17:43.017
No! You must not!

00:17:43.395 --> 00:17:45.260
You can let her in here.

00:17:46.532 --> 00:17:49.399
Yes, and that blue autonomous soldier, too.

00:17:50.702 --> 00:17:52.533
You take care of the tank for me.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.164
Understood.

00:18:04.149 --> 00:18:05.616
What are you thinking about?

00:18:11.824 --> 00:18:12.984
What about you?

00:18:14.693 --> 00:18:16.456
What are you thinking about?

00:18:26.205 --> 00:18:28.537
Who are you thinking about?

00:18:44.423 --> 00:18:46.391
Bogie, I've finished up over here.

00:18:47.059 --> 00:18:47.923
Same here.

00:18:48.026 --> 00:18:49.254
Join up with us as soon as you can.

00:18:49.895 --> 00:18:52.261
Wait, you're not coming to pick me up?

00:19:02.875 --> 00:19:05.343
There don't seem to be any
guards for the time being.

00:19:05.711 --> 00:19:06.405
So...

00:19:17.256 --> 00:19:20.953
Man, it's still easier to move around in the flesh.

00:19:22.928 --> 00:19:25.590
Smoke grenades and... these are flash grenades.

00:19:26.732 --> 00:19:30.600
I'll signal you if I use them, so watch your eyes.

00:19:43.749 --> 00:19:47.048
There's nothing here, but there's a presence.

00:19:47.386 --> 00:19:48.614
What do you mean?

00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:51.287
There's something really huge...

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:55.794
It's huge, but the reading
I'm getting is strangely weak.

00:19:55.794 --> 00:20:00.731
No, it's not weak, it's spread wide and thin.

00:20:01.967 --> 00:20:03.127
What could it be?

00:20:05.003 --> 00:20:06.436
Blood vessels?

00:20:06.905 --> 00:20:08.770
No, nerves?

00:20:09.007 --> 00:20:12.499
This place is covered with nanomachines.

00:20:12.778 --> 00:20:16.982
They've fused and assimilated
with the original material...

00:20:16.982 --> 00:20:20.042
...at a molecular level, and they've
probably changed the material itself.

00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:25.152
You could say this facility is
an artificial pseudo-life form.

00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:28.526
Just as Blue Breaker said,

00:20:28.627 --> 00:20:31.357
this fortress permeated by a strange silence...

00:20:31.663 --> 00:20:36.268
...was as if it consisted of this
mass of nanomachines...

00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:39.135
...that had been organized
into one giant life form.

00:20:40.572 --> 00:20:44.770
Honoka could definitely sense
their distinctive flow of chi.

00:20:46.111 --> 00:20:47.976
A very large flow,

00:20:48.413 --> 00:20:50.813
and yet somehow weak and fragile.

00:20:51.283 --> 00:20:55.014
Could this be Rona Fauna's chi?

00:20:59.124 --> 00:20:59.886
They've come inside.

00:21:00.359 --> 00:21:02.054
You let them in.

00:21:02.227 --> 00:21:03.216
Yes.

00:21:03.962 --> 00:21:05.395
I let them in.

00:21:06.632 --> 00:21:09.032
I want to see her.

00:21:09.668 --> 00:21:16.335
I want... to see more... of her... fighting.

00:21:19.544 --> 00:21:20.408
Rona?

00:21:21.346 --> 00:21:22.711
What's wrong, Rona?

00:21:26.184 --> 00:21:28.709
How long do I intend to keep this up?

00:21:30.222 --> 00:21:32.782
The answer is, as long as I have time.

00:21:34.259 --> 00:21:36.159
As long as time allows.

00:21:37.763 --> 00:21:38.855
I...

00:21:42.334 --> 00:21:43.995
...want to remain like this.

00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:56.581
An intersection waiting for morning...
Asa o matteiru kousaten ga

00:21:56.581 --> 00:22:00.652
...cradling an abandoned cat that wandered in.
Mayoikonda sute-neko o daiteiru

00:22:00.652 --> 00:22:03.188
Red and green and yellow.
Aka to ao to kiiro

00:22:03.188 --> 00:22:06.214
It is simply gentle.
Sore wa tada yasashii

00:22:06.858 --> 00:22:10.329
Stopping just after dawn,
Akegata-sugi ni furiyanda

00:22:10.329 --> 00:22:14.333
a misty rain made a screen of water.
Kosame ga tsukutta mizu no sukuriin ga

00:22:14.333 --> 00:22:16.902
Until that time when it dries,
Kawaku sono toki made

00:22:16.902 --> 00:22:20.065
it is simply gentle.
Sore wa tada yasashii

00:22:20.138 --> 00:22:23.608
More than small coincidences like that,
Sonna chiisana guuzen yori mo

00:22:23.608 --> 00:22:27.012
the fact that you are there...
Kimi ga soko ni iru koto ga

00:22:27.012 --> 00:22:30.482
...cannot be a small thing, I think.
Chiisai hazu ga nai to omounda

00:22:30.482 --> 00:22:34.111
Even though it's obvious.
Atarimae nandakedo

00:22:35.787 --> 00:22:42.561
It must be sad not to have anyone.
Daremo inai to kanashii koto deshou

00:22:42.561 --> 00:22:49.262
Now, come on out to where the sun is shining.
Saa hi no ataru basho e dete-oide

00:22:49.501 --> 00:22:56.341
Even the several incidents that trouble you...
Kimi o komaraseru ikutsuka no dekigoto mo

00:22:56.341 --> 00:23:01.176
...are coincidences of yesterdays past.
Kinou izen no guuzen nanda yo

00:23:03.148 --> 00:23:08.745
Though, I'm sure you actually know that already.
Hontou wa wakatteru to omou kedo

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.889
Preview

00:23:17.262 --> 00:23:19.164
As the fighting grew more intense,

00:23:19.164 --> 00:23:23.368
Bogie was cornered by the Tank Killer,
an anti-tank attack chopper...

00:23:23.368 --> 00:23:25.529
...and he was in the crosshairs of the final shot.

00:23:26.204 --> 00:23:31.073
And before me stood Blue Breaker,
turning his gun on me.

00:23:31.977 --> 00:23:36.107
The scent of death and defeat
permeated this place right then.

00:23:36.782 --> 00:23:40.309
Next time on
The Third - The Girl With The Blue Eye,

00:23:40.419 --> 00:23:42.053
episode 20, "Facing Down Death".

00:23:42.053 --> 00:23:43.422
Facing Down Death
episode 20, "Facing Down Death".

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:44.912
